From: AP-action local patch
Subject: [PATCH] shortcut-fe: fix use-after-free of the cached conntrack

fast-classifier keeps a raw struct nf_conn pointer (sfe_connection.ct) for
every offload entry and relies on the conntrack-destroy notifier to remove
the entry.  When a 5-tuple is reused (or the destroy notification misses the
entry) that pointer goes stale, and

  fast_classifier_update_protocol(conn->sic, conn->ct)

then dereferences freed memory through nf_ct_net(ct) ->
net->ct.nf_ct_proto.tcp.  Observed on ramips/mt7621 (MSG1500, MT7621):

  CPU 3 Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 000012c3
  epc : fast_classifier_recv+0xe04 [fast_classifier]   (inlined
        fast_classifier_update_protocol -> nf_tcp_pernet ->
        tn->tcp_no_window_check; 0x788 + 0x3a == 0x7c2 == BadVA - 0x0b01)
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt

The entry is looked up with the 5-tuple of the packet being processed, so
use that packet's (referenced) conntrack instead of the cached snapshot.

Ported from AP-action-IPQ 7337ea2 / efba8ce.
Applied by core.sh apply_sfe_live_conntrack_fix (add-openwrt-sfe-2410).
--- a/shortcut-fe/fast-classifier/src/fast-classifier.c
+++ b/shortcut-fe/fast-classifier/src/fast-classifier.c
@@ -1061,7 +1061,14 @@
 			if (conn->offload_permit || conn->hits >= offload_at_pkts) {
 				DEBUG_TRACE("OFFLOADING CONNECTION, TOO MANY HITS\n");
 
-				if (fast_classifier_update_protocol(conn->sic, conn->ct) == 0) {
+				/*
+				 * conn->ct is a snapshot taken when this SFE entry was created.
+				 * The conntrack it points to can already be gone (expired
+				 * connection / reused 5-tuple); nf_ct_net() would then read
+				 * freed memory and panic the box.  Use the conntrack of the
+				 * packet that is being processed here instead.
+				 */
+				if (fast_classifier_update_protocol(conn->sic, ct) == 0) {
 					spin_unlock_bh(&sfe_connections_lock);
 					fast_classifier_incr_exceptions(FAST_CL_EXCEPTION_UPDATE_PROTOCOL_FAIL);
 					DEBUG_TRACE("UNKNOWN PROTOCOL OR CONNECTION CLOSING, SKIPPING\n");
